From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 10:09:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Track which pathfinder goals are running with a flag

onUpdateTasks asked executingTaskEntries.contains() once per task entry,
and canUse asked it again for every other entry - twice per entry, since
canUse is called on both sides of the restart check. A mob with n goals
and m of them running did O(n*n*m) reference comparisons every third
tick, for every mob in every loaded chunk.

The list is only touched inside this class - two removes in the goal
setup, one add, and one iterator removal - so a flag on the entry
answers the same question in a single load. The entry can never be in
the list twice, because the add is only reached after the entry has been
removed or was never in it.

A live capture put the goal selector at 8 of the 30 samples that landed
anywhere in entity ticking, the largest cluster there.

PathfinderGoalSelectorTest drives the real selector and a transcription
of the original algorithm over the same goals for 400 ticks across 60
randomised goal sets, and requires an identical sequence of
startExecuting, resetTask and updateTask calls. The goals answer from
the tick number alone rather than from state of their own, so both runs
see the same inputs however far the implementations diverge. Dropping
either half of the flag maintenance fails both tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

